WEBVTT

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.920
Now then...

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:18.300
I think I'll simply sum up what's
happened and what's to come.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.020
The Holy Grail of Heavenly Light
that Soul Howl seeks...

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.270
"Holy Grail of Heavenly Light"

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.270
To know where to find
the materials to make it,

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:26.650
"Level 1"
"Level 2"
"Level 3"

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:29.270
"Level 1"
"Level 2"
"Level 3"

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:29.270
we need to go to the bottom level

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:32.820
of a huge archive called
Fool the Wunderkammer.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:33.900
"Firefly Glowstone"

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.490
"Firefly Glowstone"

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.490
The firefly glowstone we need to go there

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:40.740
was obtained by Garrett and
the Dark Knight last time...

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:45.710
Next, it's finally time for me to head
for Fool the Wunderkammer.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:50.050
Alcait Academy, huh?

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:57.640
The entrance to Fool the Wunderkammer
is under this academy, but...

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:08.940
Ah, youth!

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:11.020
Hey, you there!

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:16.150
Are you interested in the academy?

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.540
"Episode 7
'I Am the Strongest!'"

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:53.340
"Episode 7
'I Am the Strongest!'"

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:53.340
Oh, did I startle you?

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:57.300
I'm Hinata, one of the
teachers at this academy.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.380
You are?

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:00.010
I am Mira.

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:03.140
Those ears... So she's one of the Miao.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:06.180
Mira? That's a cute name!

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:09.560
Those are the fashionable
magical girl-style clothes, right?

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:12.900
Since you're wearing a robe-type, does
that mean you want to become a mage?

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.320
No, I'm already a mage.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.070
Eep?!

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:20.780
I'm becoming rather used to getting
this sort of reaction from people.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:27.330
I had no idea! Sorry. Oh, may I ask
what kind of mage you are?

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:30.580
Mm, I'm a summoner...

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:35.090
What is that indescribable
look on your face?!

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:38.380
S-Sorry. That's what I am, too.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:41.340
I teach evocation magic at this academy.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.340
Oh, is that so?

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:47.890
I only have... a few students now, though.

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:53.400
A-Ah. Now that you mention it,
as far as I can see here,

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:57.480
it seems that no one is
learning evocation magic.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:02.200
Without students, a teacher can
only roam adrift like a jellyfish...

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.240
That's rough!

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:07.830
But! Master Cleos, the acting
Elder of the Tower of Evocation,

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:12.790
has been burning the midnight oil putting
old contract methods into practice.

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:14.040
Cleos?

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:17.000
It seems the equipment and
Blasting Stones entrusted to him

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.460
are being put to good use...

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:21.300
The success rate is supposed
to be amazing, too!

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:24.720
So I'm sure our time will come soon!

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:30.770
Mm, I wish there was
something I could do as well.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:33.020
This is... a user's bangle, right?!

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:35.100
It's proof of a high-level adventurer!

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:37.230
W-Well, yeah...

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:42.320
Me, I have contracts with Dark Knights,
Holy Knights, Hell Hounds,

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:46.820
Salamanders, Carbuncles, and Wyverns.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.740
That's the most basic of lineups.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:53.460
Mira, I wonder, have you
contracted with any other spirits?

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:56.790
Well, strictly speaking, I have, but...

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:01.210
Please! Help me out a little bit!

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:07.090
The Mage Arts Review?

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:10.720
Yes. It's a monthly symposium
where each department

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:12.770
competes and presents spells...

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:14.310
Depending on how you're rated,

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:16.850
you might gain greater access
to academy facilities

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:19.900
or be allocated more research funds.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.520
I see.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:26.860
But the Evocation Department has
ranked last these last few years and...

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:30.490
The spirits I can summon
are good little spirits,

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:32.870
but in the end, I don't
have that many types,

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:35.870
and they're not
new or flashy, so...

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:36.830
That's rough!

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:41.460
That's why, if we summon a new spirit
that no one's seen before,

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:44.550
I feel like we could get
ranked a bit better.

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:52.510
Originally my goal was Fool
the Wunderkammer,

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:56.480
but when I see evocation magic
in such a declined state,

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:59.310
I can't just let that be.

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:02.150
I got it. Say no more.

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:03.980
So, all I have to do is go to this Review

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:07.900
and show them what evocation
magic can do, right?

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:08.990
Mira!

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:11.490
Well, well, Ms. Hinata.

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:14.490
You brought a child with you?
You seem awfully confident.

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:18.620
I-It's okay. This child is our
representative this time.

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:21.420
Representative? That child?

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:25.050
I see! It's only natural that a child's
magic would be lacking.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:27.630
And you'll be saved the embarrassment!

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:32.930
Well, you just do your best.

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:37.140
Our Sorcery Department will take
first place yet again, though.

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:42.650
Good grief...

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:45.030
Who the hell was that?

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:48.740
W-Well, his name is Caerus Berling.

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:52.740
He's heir to the Berling family,
a distinguished family of mages.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:55.080
He's a typical uppity aristocrat.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:58.160
B-But his skills as a mage are real.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:00.210
Since he came into the picture,

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:03.340
the Sorcery Department has
monopolized the number one spot.

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:10.470
Someone with moderate skills,
but not the emotional maturity to match.

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:13.800
You find his sort everywhere you go.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:22.020
Today is... today is different.

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:24.270
I don't know how far we can go,

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:27.860
but with Mira, the future
of evocation magic...

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:33.070
Huh? Why are you making
such a tortured face?!

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:38.790
No, I was thinking of summoning something
as big and flashy as possible,

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:41.460
but the venue is unexpectedly small.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:43.710
If I summon him in a place like this,

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:46.590
he'll fill every nook and cranny.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:48.380
Every nook and cranny?

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:51.300
Ugh, what should I summon?

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.510
A summon that's really something...

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:55.010
"Some-mon"

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:55.010
A some-mon...

00:07:55.010 --> 00:08:01.600
She has enough confidence to make puns...
so I'll believe in Mira!

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:07.610
Thank you for waiting! We will
now hold the Mage Arts Review!

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:10.400
Once again,
I'll explain the rules briefly.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:13.320
Each representative is given ten minutes.

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:15.910
They will present their
spells during that time.

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:18.120
Attack-type spells will target
this armor dummy

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:20.790
that is specialized to
withstand special effects.

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:23.540
I'd like each department to do their best.

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:26.750
So, we'll start the judging with
the Sorcery Department,

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:30.170
which received the
highest score last time.

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:32.010
Representative, come forward!

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:35.680
"Sorcery Department"

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:38.640
Last time, by using amazing water magic,

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:42.180
the Sorcery Department put up a
high score that crushed the others.

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:46.020
I'm also looking forward to
seeing what kind of magic

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:47.810
will be shown in this review!

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:49.320
Hey, you.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.150
Yes?

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:54.700
Not just "last time."
"Last time, once again."

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.070
Y-Yes.

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:58.200
My sincere apologies.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:00.290
This is the problem with you commoners.

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:05.250
Thank you for finding time
in your busy schedules

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:07.000
to come here on this occasion.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:09.210
Well then, I'll show you right away!

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:12.260
The brilliance of sorcery!

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:16.340
Raging heavenly fire that
burns away all it touches!

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:25.310
Army of flames flying in the sky!

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:29.730
Army? Coming from him,
it ticks me off somehow...

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:34.490
Obey your king and destroy the enemy!

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:39.530
Th-The Sorcery Department
really is tough...

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:41.530
They're crude spells.

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:44.790
The impact points and timing
are all over the place.

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:49.000
Yeah... but this is how
the Reviews go now.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.540
Practicality is a secondary concern.

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:53.380
Easy-to-understand and
flashy techniques do well.

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:56.300
Easy-to-understand and flashy?

00:09:56.300 --> 00:10:01.220
Then that settles it.
I know who to summon.

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:04.970
"Holy Magic Department"

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:14.820
"Divination Department"

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:27.870
"Immortal Arts Department"

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:37.010
"Exorcism Department"

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:45.140
"Demonology Department"

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:52.900
"Necromancy Department"

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:03.830
Moving on, let's have the Evocation
Department representative.

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:06.750
Good grief. It's finally my turn!

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:09.120
Mira...

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:13.880
Don't worry. This level of magic
is like child's play.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.960
Okay, I'm counting on you!

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:20.340
Who's that?

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:21.470
She's not one of our students.

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:23.510
She's still a child.

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:27.810
Bound Arcana?

00:11:27.810 --> 00:11:31.940
An advanced skill only high-level
summoners should be able to use.

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:33.940
What is that girl?

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:42.360
My goodness! Mark of the Rosary!

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:46.660
If you hear this voice,
if this feeling reaches you,

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:49.410
will you awaken for me?

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:51.960
I want you to let me hear that voice.

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:55.040
I want you to sing with that voice.

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.840
Your timbre that echoes
like the shimmer of bells.

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:01.170
I wish for it once more,
here and now.

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:04.800
"Evocation: Diva"

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:27.780
Oh! I finally get to see you, Maestro.

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:31.250
Mm. It's been a long time, Leticia.

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:34.460
Maestro... did you shrink?

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:36.290
No, not exactly shrunk...

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:39.300
"Maestro"

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:39.300
I think that I've changed a lot.

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:40.840
Is that so?

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:44.720
She really hasn't changed at all
since when this was a game.

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:46.430
Oh, that's right.

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:49.510
I'm writing a song about you, Maestro.

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:52.390
The lyrics aren't set yet, but...

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:54.640
We can do that another time.

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:58.770
Instead, could you let me hear
"Melodia of Fresh Verdure"?

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:03.030
I shall do as you request, Maestro.

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:53.450
What a beautiful singing voice...

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:58.380
It's like a heavenly orchestra playing
the instruments of the gods.

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:22.940
"Melodia of Fresh Verdure"

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:22.940
is a song that heals the soul.

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:26.070
It seems to have had
an outstanding effect.

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:29.660
Thank you very much, everyone!

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:32.080
Now, for the clincher.

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:36.450
Leticia, the "Requiem of Rage"
for that dummy.

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:39.500
As you request.

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:47.550
M-Mira! That just now...

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:52.260
Don't be so surprised.
It's spirit magic that uses the voice.

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:55.560
Spirit magic that uses the voice...

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:58.270
I had no idea there were
summon spirits like that...

00:14:58.270 --> 00:15:01.100
Evocation magic is more than just
summoning something

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:03.440
and throwing it at your opponent.

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:08.280
Depending on what you summon,
it infinitely expands how you fight.

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:11.240
That's what evocation magic is.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:14.280
Splendid!

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:25.710
Thanks for your hard work.

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:30.010
Let me listen to that song about me next
time, when we have a quiet moment.

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:31.260
Okay!

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:35.600
That little brat!

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:39.480
Wait, everyone!
Don't you think this is strange?

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:43.860
Is it possible for a child like this
to use such advanced magic?

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:46.650
She must be using some kind of trick!

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:49.570
He has a point. Was that evocation magic?

00:15:49.570 --> 00:15:51.820
And yeah, when you get
down to it, she is a child.

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:53.910
If you're willing to go that far,

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:58.120
instead of by judgement,
why not settle this with a duel?

00:15:58.120 --> 00:16:00.620
Caerus Berling.

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:08.130
And now, we will commence the special
judgment match! Participants, bow!

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:12.050
Bow? Umm...

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:13.510
Like this?

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:18.390
Mira! That's what you do
when you're wearing a long skirt!

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:21.940
Both participants, at the ready!

00:16:21.940 --> 00:16:23.350
Begin!

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:29.230
Army of flames flying in the sky,
obey your king...

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:38.660
What? What's happening?

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:44.080
Hey, what about that verdict?

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:48.290
Oh! Winner, evocation
magic representative!

00:16:57.550 --> 00:17:01.770
You're kidding me! Summoning
six Dark Knights in an instant?

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:02.850
Impossible!

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:05.100
You must have a collaborator!

00:17:14.650 --> 00:17:17.070
I am the strongest!

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:22.540
--Where in the world did you
learn those spells?

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:23.500
--Thank you very much!
--Where in the world did you
learn those spells?

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.710
--Thank you very much!
--Please teach me
evocation magic, too!

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:28.040
Master Cleos?

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:30.710
Oh, you were watching?

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:34.670
Would you mind coming here again later,
once things quiet down?

00:17:34.670 --> 00:17:35.970
Huh?

00:17:38.510 --> 00:17:41.720
What? What was that now? What?

00:17:41.720 --> 00:17:43.430
What the...?

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:47.690
Hey, Mira, you came just like I asked.

00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:52.730
Cleos. If you were watching,
you could have called out to me sooner.

00:17:52.730 --> 00:17:55.240
The one who was with you earlier,

00:17:55.240 --> 00:18:00.080
if I recall correctly, was Amalatte,
acting Elder of the Tower of Necromancy?

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:03.870
"Amalatte"

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:03.870
Yes, I asked her to step away for a while.

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:08.170
As a summoner, I needed to see
you about an important matter.

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:09.420
See me?

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:13.050
First, could I ask you to duel me as well?

00:18:15.510 --> 00:18:18.680
As the acting Elder of
the Tower of Evocation,

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:21.350
I'm interested in your abilities.

00:18:22.390 --> 00:18:26.850
You must have heard from Solomon
about why I came to this academy.

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:30.150
Fool the Wunderkammer, right? I know.

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:34.780
But before that,
I simply have to be certain!

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:41.490
Compressing the summoning process...

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:44.120
I suppose it's no surprise
he can do that much!

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:50.290
I may not look it,
but I am the acting Elder.

00:18:54.590 --> 00:19:00.140
Depending on what you summon,
the possibilities are endless. Right?

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:02.800
I see, you are a good student.

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:06.640
But I was still one move ahead of you.

00:19:10.190 --> 00:19:12.520
Don't think this is the end.

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:23.990
I yield.

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:29.580
I had no idea you'd already
deployed that many spells.

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:32.210
What speed and accuracy!

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:35.420
So, in the earlier duel,
you were still pulling your punches?

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:39.670
You could say that. I couldn't exactly
fight in earnest against a student.

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:42.050
Well, you were excellent as well.

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:45.260
It only took that little boy
being surrounded by Dark Knights

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:47.310
for him to foam at the mouth and collapse.

00:19:47.310 --> 00:19:50.230
I would certainly hope not to
be lumped in with a student...

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:53.730
But then, from where you stand,
I suppose we're about the same.

00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:59.900
Welcome back, Master Danblf.

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:02.820
Having dueled you myself,
I am certain now.

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:05.280
To use that many evocation spells,

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:08.410
there's no doubt I'm dealing
with Master Danblf himself.

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:11.330
No, that's what my teacher taught me.

00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:15.790
I don't know about the others,
but my eyes, those of the acting Elder,

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:17.550
can't be deceived.

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:25.970
Indeed, I am the real Danblf...

00:20:25.970 --> 00:20:27.310
I thought so.

00:20:27.310 --> 00:20:30.520
But you have become so much more adorable.

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:33.850
Do not ask about that.

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:37.190
As I thought, it's no
good going like this.

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:40.690
When this matter is cleared up,
Mariana should also be...

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:43.820
Well then, Master Dan-- Oh, no.

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:46.660
Shall I call you Miss Mira here?

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:50.950
Now that my suspicions have been resolved,
let's move on to the main subject.

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:53.500
Fool the Wunderkammer...

00:20:57.130 --> 00:21:01.300
What's wrong, Ms. Hinata?
Please relax more.

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:03.590
This is your long-awaited
victory celebration.

00:21:03.590 --> 00:21:06.430
Too much happened in one day.

00:21:06.430 --> 00:21:11.020
"Too much" is an understatement!
I got ranked first in the Review,

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:14.440
I've met the acting Elder,
and furthermore,

00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:19.820
Mira turned out to be the pupil of
Master Danblf, the One-Man Army...

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:24.070
Miss Mira, you also make sure
not to drink too much.

00:21:24.070 --> 00:21:26.320
It will affect tomorrow's work.

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:30.660
Don't worry, this is apple au lait,
not alcohol.

00:21:30.660 --> 00:21:33.160
Umm, tomorrow's work?

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:36.750
Yes, I have some business
in the underground archive.

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:39.960
I told the academy director about it.

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:41.920
We can go in right away.

00:21:41.920 --> 00:21:45.760
Well then, I have some preparations to
make, so I'll excuse myself for tonight.

00:21:45.760 --> 00:21:47.180
W-Wait please!

00:21:47.180 --> 00:21:49.720
Would you please let me come with you?

00:21:49.720 --> 00:21:51.970
Umm, sort of like for future reference.

00:21:51.970 --> 00:21:54.140
I feel seeing the two
of you in actual battle

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:57.350
is something I'll need going forward...

00:21:57.350 --> 00:21:59.560
Mm, I don't mind.

00:22:14.950 --> 00:22:20.000
Well then, this is welcome
to Wunderkammer.
